{
 "about": "Play fingerprints: per game, the SHA-1 (16 hex digits) of its state hashes in order, joined by newlines. First recorded by the JavaScript engine (2026-10-27) before it was retired; re-recorded 2026-10-28 when each card in the bots' search got its own count of targets to sample (designer); sets c, d and e re-recorded the same day without the rule variants decisions had settled (swayRequired, payInFull, fightHalf, winnerLoss). Re-recorded again 2026-10-28 when the trophy bot began planning its hand (designer), when its one-step values lost their jitter, when it kept 12 moves for its play-outs, when passing went off by default (designer), and when Steal Their Playbook changed (D30). Regenerate with `motw fingerprint ... digests=1` only when a change is meant to change play; and for the fuller start (D32) and the round-end log line without passing; and for D33's defaults (shifts bring tokens, 30 tokens a faction, threshold 30, the thinner start); and for D36 (The Gate's readings split its ends, and Sci-Fi pays when it is at either end); and for D38 (nightfall tokens replace growth); and for D39 (Steal Their Playbook takes any played card into your hand); and for D40 (threshold 10 per player); and for State Park and Occult Camp swapping places on the board (designer, prototype layout); and for D41 (the last round ends after its fights); and for D42 (threshold 20); and for 2 standing with every other faction (D43); and for no marked cards (D44); and for growth's favourites (JSON key renamed from leaders; play unchanged); and for D45: unsuited cards give 2 wild sway; and for D46: unlimited faction pools; and set votes added (2026-11-03) so rounds as votes is covered; and for play-outs carried through nightfall and growth to the round's end (they had stopped at nightfall, before the fights and the vote); and for rplan on by default (designer): every seat in the play-outs follows its own remembered hand plan; and for rplan and tiekeep on by default (designer), and the fingerprint games given the table (every seat's profile and memory) as the runner and the live game give it; and for D47: two starting sway on each affinity location. And for the bots' end-of-round vote reading (designer, 2026-11-05: never opening presence; replacing drain, trend, look and vknown). Re-recorded the same day: play-outs and the draft read the votes from the seat's remembered play-out reading. Re-recorded 2026-11-06: one bot with dials by default (designer: one bot type with tunable options; hedging on a spectrum).",
